{"id": "EUVD-2026-90687", "enisaUuid": "4060c00b-d87c-324f-9e3c-72d6ef0e9bde", "description": "Obot 0.21.1 through 0.24.1 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows authenticated users to reach MCP servers because the checkUI deny list omits the /mcp-connect-composite/ route. Basic-role users with a composite MCP ID can proxy requests through mcpGateway.Proxy to invoke tools on MCP servers restricted by Access Control Rules.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T10:42:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T14:35:10", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/obot-platform/obot/security/advisories/GHSA-6fwv-3h4c-37j9", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/obot-0.21.1-through-0.24.1-authorization-bypass-via-mcp-connect-composite-route"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-103758", "GHSA-x6jv-4hp7-3vj9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ce59fb1-c59d-3637-b080-7da0e2d76e2b", "product": {"name": "obot", "vendor": {"name": "obot-platform"}}, "product_version": "0.21.1 \u22640.24.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a7d44ec1-8971-3d82-a072-1bec2f53df47", "vendor": {"name": "obot-platform"}}], "isExploited": false}